<title>RUSSIA: MICEX to trade Swiss franc, Italian lira.</title>
<headline>MICEX to trade Swiss franc, Italian lira.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Moscow Interbank Currency Exchange (MICEX) plans to start trading the Swiss franc on January 27 and the Italian lira on February 3, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>Nikita Zolotaryov said the currencies would be traded each day. Minimum lots are 1,000 Swiss francs and one million Italian lire.</p>
<p>MICEX currently trades dollars, marks, sterling, French francs, Ukranian hryvnia, Kazakh tenge and Belarus roubles.</p>
